 =\frac{121\binom{20}{10}}{21\cdot2^{20}}
 =\frac{22\,355\,476}{22\,020\,096}>1.$$ Thus $K$ violates <a href="#eq:proposed-bound" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:proposed-bound">[eq:proposed-bound]</a> in dimension twenty.

Let $P\subset\mathbb R^d$, $d\ge2$, be a full-dimensional convex polytope. For each facet $F$, let $s_F$ be its $(d-1)$-dimensional volume and $\nu_F$ its outward unit normal. Then $$\label{eq:facet}
 h_{\Pi P}(u)=\frac12\sum_Fs_F|\langle\nu_F,u\rangle|,
 \qquad u\in\mathbb R^d,$$ and therefore $$\label{eq:zonotope}
 \Pi P=\sum_F
 \left[-\frac{s_F\nu_F}{2},\frac{s_F\nu_F}{2}\right].$$

Let $A\subset\mathbb R^r$ and $B\subset\mathbb R^s$ be full-dimensional convex polytopes, where $r,s\ge2$. In the orthogonal product space $\mathbb R^{r+s}=\mathbb R^r\times\mathbb R^s$, $$\label{eq:product-body}
 \Pi(A\times B)=(|B|\Pi A)\times(|A|\Pi B).$$ In particular, $$\label{eq:multiplicative}
 R_{r+s}(A\times B)=R_r(A)R_s(B).$$
